the Batman vs Superman Easter eggs that  flew over your head with the running  time of two and a half hours Batman vs  Superman dawn of Justice has a lot going  on we've gone over all 153 minutes with  a fine-tooth comb and picked out the  best and biggest Easter eggs to give you  hints of what to look for in the movie  here's a spoiler build guide to all the  DC Comics goodies peppered throughout  the film one more time for anyone who's  not paying attention major spoilers  ahead still here great let's dive in  Darkseid is coming Bruce Wayne's  nightmare vision which occurs while he's  asleep at his bad desk hints that  something major looming on the PC movie  horizon fans of the comics will  recognize the flying creatures in this  scene as parademons the nasty comics  creatures who served the intergalactic  uber villain known as Darkseid you can  also see Darkseid - Omega symbol carved  into the ground at the beginning of  Bruce's vision and Luthor seems to  directly reference his impending arrival  when he threatens he's coming at the end  of the movie but that's not the only  hints of Darkseid presence we get out of  Batman vs Superman mother buys when  Wonder Woman takes a tour through Lex  Luthor's metahuman files we get our best  looks yet at the future members of the  Justice League including the flash  Aquaman and Cyborg in particular cyborgs  origin told via lab footage that shows  him being booted up for the first time  has even more to offer fans than just  the beginnings of a major superhero  that's because we can a look at what  seems to be a mother box a super  powerful supercomputer ripped right from  the pages of Jack Kirby's new god saga  just like Batman's vision of the future  the mother box has major ties with  Darkseid and the aliens of new Genesis  and apocalypse since it looks like  cyborgs creation has direct ties to New  Gods technology just like the new  version of his origin in the comics from  2011 expect the hero to play a pretty  big role in the DC extended universe  riddle me this  Batman's troubled past is felt more than  seen or discussed in Batman  Superman dawn of justice but Snyder's  fondness for referencing comics war can  be seen in the building where the  showdown between the two heroes goes  down if you look carefully you can spot  what looks a lot like some graffiti left  behind by the Riddler or perhaps some of  his henchmen  might we see him in future DC movies and  will Jim Carrey reprised the role cagey  beast  Lex Luthor has a high-ranking Hegeman  and Batman vs Superman named Anatole  kanai's him played by Kalin Moby and  although he doesn't look anything like  he does in the comics DC fans will  recognize that as the real name of the  villain known as cagey beast could we be  seeing two knives EV in a different form  later on considering his fate in this  movie getting exploded after Batman  shoots at the flamethrower he's wearing  on his back it's a good bet that he'll  be more inclined to wear something  closer to his comic book costume in  future appearances assuming of course he  hasn't simply been incinerated mercy  graves that's no ordinary employee  bringing Sods corpse to Lex Luthor fans  of Superman the animated series will  recognize the character of Mercy graves  played here by calico moto Luthor's  personal assistant and bodyguard she  became a fan favorite during the run of  the series and it's exciting to see her  brought to the big screen in such a  major movie of course unless we  misunderstood the scene where she's  inside the Senate building that explodes  about halfway through the movie we might  not get much more mercy in future DC  film flicks oh well metallo before the  movie came out it was rumored that  Batman vs Superman dawn of Justice would  feature an appearance by metallo the  comics villain who goes from life as a  soldier to a life of crime after having  his body rebuilt with kryptonite powered  cyborg parts that didn't quite happen  probably because of how many other  details were crammed into its running  time yet if you watch the closing  credits you'll see that one of the  technicians demonstrating the effects of  kryptonite in Luthor's lab is named  Emmet Vale  which just happens to be the name of the  scientist who filled metallo watch for  the metal man to make his debut in a  future DC extended universe bill Jimmy  Olsen as much fun as Zack Snyder clearly  has calling back to the comics he isn't  above changing things up when it suits  him  case in point Jimmy Olsen's brief and  ultimately tragic cameo in Batman vs  Superman dawn of Justice early in the  film when Lois travels through the  fictional country of Nairobi Africa for  a story she's accompanied by a  photographer who turns out to be a CIA  scoop and is quickly put to death by the  warlord she's interviewing according to  remarks Snyder made during his press  corps for the film that's actually Jimmy  Olsen  although Snyder didn't think there was  any room in the DC Cinematic Universe  for him the director decided putting one  of Superman's best friends in the movie  and killing him off would be a way to  have fun with the character Zod of  Pandora we saw a return from Man of  Steel's bad guy General Zod albeit in  the form of a corpse and then a CGI  monster while the trailers showed that  to be the case months before the movie  dropped the little robots inside the  Kryptonian ship did give us another cool  little Easter egg we find out that Zod  comes from the city of Kandor which is  better known to comic fans as the bottle  city of Kandor the capital city of  Krypton candor is shrunken and stolen by  the Superman villain Brainiac and is  added to his intergalactic collection of  artifacts after Superman and Brainiac  square off Kandor ends up under  Superman's protection at the fortress of  solitude hopefully we get a chance to  see a movie version of the classic  Superman villain with candor in tow The  Dark Knight Returns if you've watched  Watchmen you know that Zack Snyder likes  recreating comic panels in his film  adaptations and Batman vs Superman dawn  of Justice is loaded with callbacks to  one of its biggest inspirations the  Frank Miller graphic novel The Dark  Knight Returns it starts early with the  movie's depiction of Bruce Wayne's  parents being killed a shot of Miss  Wayne's pearls around the muggers gun is  a direct lit from the book and continues  throughout the movie both in the  dialogue and in the way certain shots  are lined up more than anything however  man's coward armor which he wears during  the title fight with Superman is taken  straight from Miller's iconic series  Action Comics love him or hate him  Snyder definitely enjoys paying homage  to the comics one brief example comes  during an argument between Clark Kent  and Perry White at the office of The  Daily Planet  during which white tells Kent that he  can't report on the types of stories he  wants to cover because it's not 1938  anymore as any DC fan can tell you  that's the year Superman made his first  appearance in Action Comics number one  must there be a Superman the movies  action comics reference is far from the  only nod to the Man of Steel's print an  adventure during one seen the senator  played by Holly Hunter asks must there  be a Superman it's an interesting  question and one that directly points to  a 1972 issue of the Superman comic in  which our hero is forced to face a  Tribunal for his quote crimes against  humanity since the hero is instrumental  in the defeat of doomsday and the  foundation of the Justice League this is  a question that gets answered with a  resounding yes by the end of the movie  thanks for watching subscribe to our  YouTube channel to see more videos like  the one you just watch and leave us a  comment to let us know which Easter Egg  was your favorite and any ones that you  think should have made the list
 

